Aṅguttara IV–VII: qualities, conditions, and gradations (@buddhist-an-fours-to-sevens: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @buddhism, #source @buddhist-source-numerical-discourses, #philosophy @buddhist-an-eights-to-elevens, #buddhism @buddhist-an-eights-to-elevens) { r_5ZG3GR9SQM6PSV8PBH02RFC6J7
**Read:** the books of fours through sevens in [The Numerical Discourses of the Buddha](../sources/Numerical-discourses.lingua#r_16JWQQQAWBJN7CX05AEG4WF5FR), in sequence. Complete these books rather than only reading the examples selected for a note.

Investigate how qualities and conditions are related in specific teachings. Larger lists do not necessarily describe later stages, and a useful mnemonic does not establish that the qualities have been cultivated.

**Consolidate:** Compare two related lists concerning conduct or cultivation. Distinguish a shared term from a shared function, and support the distinction with a discourse.

**Check:** show how one distinction clarifies a difficulty retained from the Saṃyutta, Majjhima, or Suttanipāta. Keep AN numbers with your examples.

**Continue:** [Aṅguttara VIII–XI: consolidation across the collections](AN-Eights-to-elevens.lingua#r_49KP60BM2H88AGXPG75ZCRXPK9).

**Return:** [Buddhism: from the path to sustained inquiry](../Buddhism.lingua#r_7P61Z6HHZNZZ8ND3DHXSFSNRRE).
